;"><span><span role="presentation"><a class="AuthorLink_author-link__rg5qj" data-tmdatatrack="author" data-testid="byline-author" href="https://www.lancs.live/authors/neil-shaw/"><strong class="Strong_strong__e2x35 __className_fe3bd2">Neil Shaw</strong></a></span> Assistant Editor</span></div></div><div class="ArticleTimestamp_dates-container__yHhr9"><span class="" data-testid="byline-publishedDate">10:47, 10 Apr 2025</span></div></div><div class="DisclosureNotice_disclosure-notice__LgLFU">This article contains affiliate links, we will receive a commission on any sales we generate from it. <a href="/affiliates/">Learn more</a></div></span></div><button type="button" class="SlideViewerButton_slide-viewer-button__BDJoG" aria-label="Open image viewer" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="image-lightbox"><div class="ImageEmbed_image-embed__0T8WX ImageEmbed_image-lead__Ti3qQ" data-testid="leadimage" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-articleid="31393021"><div class="ImageEmbed_image-container__2AIQm"><figure class="Figure_figure__Uce4f" style="--figure-aspect-ratio:1.5"><img alt="Hot cross buns could land you in trouble" loading="eager" sizes="(max-width: 508px) 508px, (max-width: 615px) 615px, 1200px" src="https://i2-prod.lancs.live/article31393021.ece/ALTERNATES/s1200f/0_GettyImages-150639036.jpg" srcSet="https://i2-prod.lancs.live/article31393021.ece/ALTERNATES/s508/0_GettyImages-150639036.jpg 508w, https://i2-prod.lancs.live/article31393021.ece/ALTERNATES/s615/0_GettyImages-150639036.jpg 615w, https://i2-prod.lancs.live/article31393021.ece/ALTERNATES/s1200f/0_GettyImages-150639036.jpg 1200w"/><div class="ImageCountLabel_view-images-label__pxKau" data-testid="image-count-label"><div data-testid="label" class="Tag_label__s0LCV label--section-color "><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" data-testid="icon-camera"><g clip-path="url(#clip0_11032_234208)"><path opacity="0.16" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M21 6H3V16C3 17.1046 3.89543 18 5 18H19C20.1046 18 21 17.1046 21 16V6ZM12 15C13.6569 15 15 13.6569 15 12C15 10.3431 13.6569 9 12 9C10.3431 9 9 10.3431 9 12C9 13.6569 10.3431 15 12 15Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M17 2L19 2M3 5H21V17C21 18.1046 20.1046 19 19 19H5C3.89543 19 3 18.1046 3 17V5ZM15 12C15 13.6569 13.6569 15 12 15C10.3431 15 9 13.6569 9 12C9 10.3431 10.3431 9 12 9C13.6569 9 15 10.3431 15 12Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g><defs><clipPath id="clip0_11032_234208"><rect width="24" height="24" fill="white"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg><span data-testid="label-text" class="Tag_text__ED20G">View Image</span></div></div></figure></div><figcaption class="ImageCaption_caption__j7HRu" data-testid="image-caption"><span class="ImageCaption_caption-header__4xmz_" data-testid="caption-header"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g clip-path="url(#clip0_209_94274)"><path opacity="0.16" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M14 4H2V10.6667C2 11.403 2.59695 12 3.33333 12H12.6667C13.403 12 14 11.403 14 10.6667V4ZM8 10C9.10457 10 10 9.10457 10 8C10 6.89543 9.10457 6 8 6C6.89543 6 6 6.89543 6 8C6 9.10457 6.89543 10 8 10Z" fill="var(--color-sem-icon-primary-default)"></path><path d="M2 3.33331H14V11.3333C14 12.0697 13.403 12.6666 12.6667 12.6666H3.33333C2.59695 12.6666 2 12.0697 2 11.3333V3.33331Z" stroke="var(--color-sem-icon-primary-default)" stroke-width="1.33333" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="2" stroke="var(--color-sem-icon-primary-default)" stroke-width="1.33333" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></circle><path d="M11.3332 1.33331L12.6665 1.33331" stroke="var(--color-sem-icon-primary-default)" stroke-width="1.33333" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g><defs><clipPath id="clip0_209_94274"><rect width="16" height="16" fill="white"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg></span><p aria-label="Hot cross buns could land you in trouble" class="ImageCaption_caption-title__ccyQU" data-testid="caption-title">Hot cross buns could land you in trouble</p></figcaption></div></button><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">If you’re hitting the road this Easter, then be wary of enjoying a hot cross bun or two before your trip. Motoring experts from <a aria-label="[object Object]Link opens in a new tab." class="TextLink_text-link__dBSS0 TextLink_enabled__dJF3l" href="https://go.skimresources.com?id=76202X1536631&amp;xs=1&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ripeinsurance.co.uk%2Fmotorhome-insurance%2F&amp;sref=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lancs.live%2Fnews%2Fmotoring%2Fmotoring-news%2Fwarning-easter-food-can-trigger-31393013" rel="nofollow" tabindex="0" target="_blank"><u>Ripe Motorhome Insurance</u></a> have warned of the lesser-known side effects of hot cross buns on a breathalyser test.</p><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">Alan Thomas, CEO of Ripe Motorhome Insurance said: “Just one bite of a hot cross bun can increase your blood alcohol level from 0 up to 0.018.</p><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">&quot;Foods that have started to ferment, such as hot cross buns containing yeast, can create trace amounts of mouth alcohol, which may show up on a breathalyser test.</p><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">“While this isn’t reflective of the actual blood alcohol level in your system, this means that consuming a hot cross bun or two could get you into hot water if pulled over and lead to an unnecessary follow-up test which is the last thing you’d want over the Easter weekend!”</p><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">But it’s not just hot cross buns which can cause a false-positive test. Other lesser-known foods and drinks which could lead to false readings:</p><ul class="UnorderedList_unordered-list__gzblI" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="unordered-list"><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Fermented drinks like kombucha</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Energy drinks</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Fermented foods like sauerkraut, kimchi and yoghurts</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Vanilla extract</li></ul><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">If you are partial to a hot cross bun during the spring season, make sure to wash it down with a glass of water before driving if you’re worried about a false-positive reading.</p><p class="Paragraph_paragraph-text__PVKlh" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="paragraph">Fermented foods like sauerkraut, kimchi, kombucha, kefir, soy sauce, or even ripe fruits can contain small amounts of alcohol due to the fermentation process. When you eat them or drink something like kombucha, trace alcohol might be present in your mouth—this is called mouth alcohol.</p><h3 class="HeadingThree_heading-three__PBHLs  __className_b5eaf9">Breathalyser sensitivity:</h3><ul class="UnorderedList_unordered-list__gzblI" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="unordered-list"><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Mouth alcohol can skew breathalyser results because most breathalysers are designed to detect ethanol on your breath, assuming it’s from the lungs (indicating blood alcohol content).</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">If you’ve just consumed something fermented, and a breath test is taken immediately after, the residual alcohol in your mouth can cause a false positive.</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">After a few minutes (usually 10–15), the mouth alcohol dissipates, and the breathalyser will give a more accurate reading.</li></ul><div class="BoxStyles_box-container__Qk3WH BoxStyles_commercial__Wo6Z4" data-testid="commercial-1" data-position="1"><div data-testid="commercial-label-mantisCarousel" class="sc-255f486b-4 lovMQD commercial-label-style"><span class="sc-255f486b-0 kRmbNa">Article continues below</span><div data-testid="ad-info" class="sc-255f486b-1 gyrzvf commercial-label-ad-info-style"></div><div id="mantis-ui-widget-1-bart" class="sc-255f486b-2 frkNWL"></div></div><div data-testid="commercial-mid-article-box-last" data-tmdatatrack="non-content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="commercial" data-tmdatatrack-index="1000" data-tmdatatrack-id="mantisCarousel" class="sc-3467c75c-0 iGxxyq"><div class="sc-3ec2e2de-0 dCTlqR"><mantis-ui-widget id="mantis-ui-widget-1" data-config="{&quot;displayAdSlots&quot;:&quot;false&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;subType&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;leaderBoardEnabled&quot;:&quot;true&quot;,&quot;adsEnabled&quot;:&quot;true&quot;}" data-testid="mantis-carousel"></mantis-ui-widget></div></div></div><h3 class="HeadingThree_heading-three__PBHLs  __className_b5eaf9">Real-world impact:</h3><ul class="UnorderedList_unordered-list__gzblI" data-tmdatatrack="content-unit" data-tmdatatrack-type="unordered-list"><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Low-level false positives might happen with certain very sensitive devices.</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Police-grade breathalysers usually involve a waiting period or multiple tests to avoid this kind of error.</li><li class="LiItem_li-item__IF4xI">Consumer devices (like personal breathalysers or ignition interlocks) might be more prone to picking up on these trace levels.</li></ul></article><section class="GooglePreferredSource_wrapper__lSRA6" data-testid="inline-google-preferred-source-ncu" data-tmdatatrack="google-preferred" data-tmdatatrack-type="article" data-tmdatatrack-id="article-google-preferred"><a data-testid="clickable" class="GooglePreferredSource_clickable__7nS3B" href="ht